course: dictionary
lesson: 13635
title: Industrious and industrial
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An industrious person works hard and keeps busy. You can spot the meaning from the clues around the word. Ants are called industrious because they carry food all day long.
explain: «Mia was industrious all week, finishing her maths and reading every night.» The clues are finishing and every night: Mia keeps going and does not stop. So industrious means hard-working and always busy. Check it: would a lazy person fit here? No, so your meaning is right.
explain: Be careful with a look-alike word. «The industrial town had tall chimneys and noisy factories.» Industrial is about factories and making goods, not about a person working hard. The two words look alike, but they mean different things, so check the sentence before you decide.
fact: Industrious means hard-working and always busy.
fact: «The industrious bees visited a hundred flowers before lunch.» Bees and ants are often called industrious.
fact: Industrious is an adjective, so it can change: more industrious, most industrious.
fact: In stories, industrious characters often contrast with lazy ones: busy Mole spring-cleaning his home, while idle Toad does very little.
fact: Industrial means about factories and making goods. It is a different word, so do not mix it up with industrious.
exercise: «Ben was industrious, sweeping the yard and stacking the wood before tea.» What does industrious mean? | *Hard-working and always busy | Hungry and tired | Lazy and asleep | Quiet and shy
exercise: Which of these animals is often called industrious? | *Ant | Cloud | Puddle | Rock
exercise: «The industrial estate was full of noisy factories.» What is industrial about? | *Factories and making goods | A person who works very hard | Hard-working ants | A gentle, quiet park
test: «Priya was industrious, always practising her piano and never giving up.» Which word is the closest in meaning to industrious? | Sleepy | Grumpy | *Hard-working | Lazy
test: In the story, Mole is industrious while Toad is the opposite. Which word describes Toad? | Busy | Clever | *Idle | Hard-working
exam: Which word fits the gap? «The ____ town had smoky chimneys and busy factories.» | *Industrial | Sleepy | Lazy | Industrious
